From: htrecomp
Subject: [PATCH] core: GetExecutablePath must not use _get_wpgmptr

_wpgmptr is a per-CRT-instance global that only the EXECUTABLE's CRT startup
populates. This TU is part of rexruntime, a SHARED library, so when a consumer
links the static CRT the DLL gets its own CRT instance in which _wpgmptr was
never initialised. _get_wpgmptr then hands a null to the invalid-parameter
handler, which in a release CRT calls __fastfail and kills the process with
STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN (0xC0000409).

__fastfail bypasses SEH, so an installed unhandled-exception filter never runs
and no crash dump is written - the process simply vanishes during startup.

GetModuleFileNameW(nullptr, ...) returns the executable's path and is correct
regardless of CRT linkage or which module calls it.

Windows-only; the POSIX implementation is unaffected.
---
diff --git a/src/core/filesystem_win.cpp b/src/core/filesystem_win.cpp
index c5a2c5d..312eda6 100644
--- a/src/core/filesystem_win.cpp
+++ b/src/core/filesystem_win.cpp
@@ -43,9 +43,38 @@ std::filesystem::path to_path(const std::u16string_view source) {
 namespace filesystem {
 
 std::filesystem::path GetExecutablePath() {
-  wchar_t* path;
-  auto error = _get_wpgmptr(&path);
-  return !error ? std::filesystem::path(path) : std::filesystem::path();
+  // GetModuleFileNameW(nullptr, ...), NOT _get_wpgmptr.
+  //
+  // _wpgmptr is a per-CRT-instance global that only the EXECUTABLE's CRT
+  // startup populates. This translation unit is part of rexruntime, a SHARED
+  // library, so when a consumer links the static CRT
+  // (CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=MultiThreaded) this DLL gets its own CRT
+  // instance in which _wpgmptr was never initialised. _get_wpgmptr then hands
+  // a null to the invalid-parameter handler, which in a release CRT calls
+  // __fastfail and kills the process with STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN
+  // (0xC0000409) before any of this function's callers can react. Because
+  // __fastfail bypasses SEH, an installed unhandled-exception filter never
+  // runs and no crash dump is produced - the process simply vanishes.
+  //
+  // GetModuleFileNameW with a null module handle returns the executable's path
+  // and is correct regardless of CRT linkage or which module calls it.
+  std::wstring buffer(MAX_PATH, L'\0');
+  for (;;) {
+    const DWORD copied =
+        GetModuleFileNameW(nullptr, buffer.data(), static_cast<DWORD>(buffer.size()));
+    if (!copied) {
+      return {};
+    }
+    if (copied < buffer.size()) {
+      buffer.resize(copied);
+      return std::filesystem::path(std::move(buffer));
+    }
+    // Truncated: the path is longer than the buffer. Grow and retry.
+    if (buffer.size() >= 32768) {
+      return {};  // beyond the extended-path limit; something is very wrong
+    }
+    buffer.resize(buffer.size() * 2);
+  }
 }
 
 std::filesystem::path GetExecutableFolder() {
